<title>ISRAEL: Israel current account deficit narrowed in quarter.</title>
<headline>Israel current account deficit narrowed in quarter.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The current account deficit in Israel's balance of payments narrowed to $1.136 billion in the first quarter of 1997, the Central Bureau of Statistics said on Thursday.</p>
<p>				  (In millions of dollars)</p>
<p>			     Q1 97	 Q4 96	  Q1 96</p>
<p>Exports		     8,035	 8,105	  7,646</p>
<p>Imports		    10,684	11,191	 10,711</p>
<p>Unilateral transfers    1,513	 3,125	  1,508</p>
<p>Surplus (deficit)	(1,136)	   38	 (1,557)</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
